\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The collapse law on 17 corpus and encoder pairs, sorted by out of sample $R^2$; the line separates the pairs that pass the diagnostic (out of sample $R^2 \ge 0.9$). $d$ is the TwoNN dimension, mean and sd over five pilots of 2{,}000 documents (and over three samples for the GTR forum corpora). $b$ and both $R^2$ come from the fit of Equation~\ref {eq:collapse} on cells with $n \le 1{,}000$; $R^2$ out is computed on cells with $n > 1{,}000$. The errors are mean absolute errors of the predicted $G$ at the largest $n$ (7{,}000, or $0.7N$), for the collapse law and for a per radius Chao and Jost extrapolation from $n = 1{,}000$.}}{6}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:collapse}{{1}{6}{The collapse law on 17 corpus and encoder pairs, sorted by out of sample $R^2$; the line separates the pairs that pass the diagnostic (out of sample $R^2 \ge 0.9$). $d$ is the TwoNN dimension, mean and sd over five pilots of 2{,}000 documents (and over three samples for the GTR forum corpora). $b$ and both $R^2$ come from the fit of Equation~\ref {eq:collapse} on cells with $n \le 1{,}000$; $R^2$ out is computed on cells with $n > 1{,}000$. The errors are mean absolute errors of the predicted $G$ at the largest $n$ (7{,}000, or $0.7N$), for the collapse law and for a per radius Chao and Jost extrapolation from $n = 1{,}000$}{table.caption.1}{}}
